<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Noël Ballay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1847–1902</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Noël Ballay was a French physician, explorer and colonial administrator. He accompanied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-savorgnan-de-brazza">Pierre Savorgnan de Brazza</a>'s expeditions in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ogooue">Ogooué</a> and Congo region from 1875, then served as lieutenant-governor of Gabon and from 1890 as the first governor of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>, making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conakry">Conakry</a> its capital. He died at Saint-Louis in 1902 while governor-general of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/noel-ballay.jpg" alt="Noël Ballay" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:No%C3%ABl_Ballay_par_Nadar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
